  "description": "Fuaran.Core.Idl — the interface-definition model: a typed description of a domain's node vocabulary (kinds, unions, enums, records, four-way optionality, a declarable node envelope, hosted slots), the schema-driven canonical encoder/decoder derived from it, a deterministic adversarial sampler over a vocabulary, the canonical `idl.json` artifact projection, and the host-neutral sanitisation floor. Fable-clean on both the encode and the decode path. The source emitters (F#, TypeScript, JSON Schema), the codegen trust boundary and the stability diff classifier ship separately as Fuaran.Core.Idl.Codegen. The engine only; a vocabulary is DATA a domain declares and owns in its own repo. FSharp.Core + Fuaran.Core.Wire only.",
